--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The engine is meant to be reused; the game's world is not. Keeping the boundary
explicit is what lets the engine stay permissively licensed without also giving
away the fiction it was built to run -- and a reader who finds the faction bible
in an open repository is entitled to know which of the two they are holding.

The boundary follows the repository layout, so it stays checkable: if a file
teaches you how the engine works, it is Apache-2.0; if it tells you what the
game *is*, it is reserved.
